PICO + RealMan Dual-Arm Teleoperation

This project includes and adapts components and design ideas from:

  TAMEn: Tactile-Aware Manipulation Engine for Closed-Loop Data
  Collection in Contact-Rich Tasks
  https://github.com/OpenDriveLab/TAMEn

TAMEn is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its authors
and contributors retain their respective copyright and attribution
notices.

Changes in this project include replacing the JAKA robot backend with a
RealMan API2/CANFD dual-arm backend, adding RealMan-specific coordinate
mapping and safety controls, and adding a direct three-camera RealSense
WebSocket-JPEG service.

The locally used tAmeR_192.168.3.6_video_v2.apk is a modified object-form
build derived from the TAMEn tAmeR application. It was re-signed for local
development and changes the video endpoint for the experiment network at
192.168.3.6:8765. It is not an original OpenDriveLab-signed release and is
not distributed in this Git repository.
